help: the trait `OpaqueEncode` is not implemented for `Tags`
  --> tests/ui/scalar_derived_not_one_value.rs:13:1
   |
13 | struct Tags(Vec<String>);
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: one value is a `String`, a `bool`, a float, a `Vec<u8>`, or an integer other than `u8`. A newtype that derives `Encrypt` over one of these is one value too.
   = note: a borrow, such as a `&str`, is not owned. Pass an owned value, such as a `String`.
   = note: the type must implement `Zeroize`, so that the value can be wiped after it is encrypted.
   = note: to encrypt each element of a `Vec` into its own `Ciphertext`, use `EncryptInto`.
   = note: to encrypt an `Option`, or a struct that derives `Encrypt`, use `keyset.encrypt_tree`. The result is a tree of ciphertexts.
   = note: to encrypt a whole `Serialize` value as one `Ciphertext`, wrap the value in `OpaqueBlob`.
help: the trait `OpaqueEncode` is implemented for `OpaqueBlob<T>`
  --> src/blob.rs
   |
   | impl<T: Serialize + Zeroize + Send + 'static> OpaqueEncode for OpaqueBlob<T> {}
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
